                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="14494252" author="agura" created="Tue, 14 Apr 2015 15:25:10 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Alexey, I can&apos;t reproduce this issue. See test (&lt;span class=&quot;nobr&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/12725253/12725253_ignite-737-test.patch&quot; title=&quot;ignite-737-test.patch attached to IGNITE-737&quot;&gt;ignite-737-test.patch&lt;sup&gt;&lt;img class=&quot;rendericon&quot; src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/link_attachment_7.gif&quot; height=&quot;7&quot; width=&quot;7&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;). Could you provide more details?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14495175" author="kuaw26" created="Wed, 15 Apr 2015 00:01:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It seems that issue does not reproduced any more.&lt;br/&gt;
Please ask Yakov - do we need to add tests developed by you for this issue to codebase and merge them if &quot;yes&quot; or just close issue if &quot;no&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14496154" author="agura" created="Wed, 15 Apr 2015 13:17:37 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Discussed with Yakov. It&apos;s not applicable for daemon node to invoke methods forXxxNodes(String cacheName). Now IllegalStateException throws when similar call occurres. Corresponding tests added. See &lt;span class=&quot;nobr&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/12725567/12725567_ignite-737.patch&quot; title=&quot;ignite-737.patch attached to IGNITE-737&quot;&gt;ignite-737.patch&lt;sup&gt;&lt;img class=&quot;rendericon&quot; src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/link_attachment_7.gif&quot; height=&quot;7&quot; width=&quot;7&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14499494" author="kuaw26" created="Fri, 17 Apr 2015 08:53:57 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Please test in ignite-737 branch.&lt;br/&gt;
ALL cache operation should be tested in VisorGUI and VisorCmd in BOTH modes: internal and external.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14502304" author="pkonstantinov" created="Mon, 20 Apr 2015 03:41:47 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;1. Cache configuration is empty for nodes started after visor&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14502315" author="pkonstantinov" created="Mon, 20 Apr 2015 04:01:52 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;2. Ask for node in case when we clear local cache&lt;br/&gt;
3. &apos;cache -clear&apos; shows different size in cache list table &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;+----+----------------------+-------------+----------------------------------------+---------------+
| 5  | dcp_1(@c5)           | PARTITIONED | [f896e2da-526a-4ce2-958f-c197593e0f00] | min: 22033    |
|    |                      |             |                                        | avg: 22033.00 |
|    |                      |             |                                        | max: 22033    |
+----+----------------------+-------------+----------------------------------------+---------------+
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;and in results table&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;Choose cache number (&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&apos;c&apos;&lt;/span&gt; to cancel) [c]: 5
Cleared cache with name: dcp_1
+======================================================+
|  Node ID8(@)  | Cache Size Before | Cache Size After |
+======================================================+
| F896E2DA(@n1) | 46751             | 0                |
+------------------------------------------------------+
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The reason is that the first table shows size taken only from one node(incorrect) and the second entire the cache(correct)&lt;br/&gt;
4. we should sum size for local cache in first table if node is not specified for &apos;cache -clear&apos;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14958931" author="kuaw26" created="Thu, 15 Oct 2015 13:50:50 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Pavel, please investigate if this issue is actual?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14962930" author="pkonstantinov" created="Mon, 19 Oct 2015 06:51:09 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;These issues are still actual:&lt;br/&gt;
1) we should ask user for node to clear local cache&lt;br/&gt;
2) &apos;cache -clear -c=@cXX&apos; shows only one node where cache was cleared but I&apos;m expected to see all nodes with cache.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
